!has(object.spec.type) || object.spec.type != 'LoadBalancer' || !has(object.spec.ports) || object.spec.ports.all(p, !((p.port >= 30000 && p.port <= 32767) || p.port == 10250))
'k3sm: LoadBalancer port ' + string(object.spec.ports.filter(p, ((p.port >= 30000 && p.port <= 32767) || p.port == 10250))[0].port) + ' is RESERVED by a k3sm wildcard listener (the NodePort range 30000-32767 and the kubelet API port 10250). k3sm binds LoadBalancer ports on 0.0.0.0 and Go sets no SO_REUSEPORT, so this Service would race a k3sm listener for the same socket — losing the kubelet API port breaks logs/exec/top on this node, and a NodePort-range collision takes down an unrelated ClusterIP. Choose a different spec.ports[].port. Only these RESERVED ports are rejected: two Services sharing an ordinary LoadBalancer port are still first-come.'
